SUMMARY:From Boy Scout to Soldier\, Simon J. Gurdal
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nSimon Gurdal was fourteen when the Germans 
 occupied his home Verviers\, Belgium in 1940. He said "all we could do was
  to hide ourselves. One day our bell rang. It was two ladies who had a six
  year old Jewish girl\, Annie. The lady said 'she's for you' and they rush
 ed away. Annie had a piece of paper in her coat pocket which read: I am a 
 Jewish girl\, please take me in and hide me." In 1944 I was 17. One of the
  boyscouts in my troop said Let's join the army. I said\, let's go. Seven 
 of us went to Saint Nicolas-Waes and soon we were in the army. We were sen
 t north to fight with British Field Marshal Montgomery in Operation Market
  Garden. One time I found myself in a foxhole with two Americans\, a Canad
 ian\, and a Polish soldier. I was wounded but went back into the fight.\n\
 nI am now an American citizen. I'm proud to wear the badge of Belgian Brig
 ade Piron. What I tell you comes from my memory but mostly from my heart.\
 n\nCome take the opportunity to meet Simon at the Main Library. No registr
 ation required.
