SUMMARY:Cove Crk/Caney Bottoms Short Loop
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**A Walk in the Park\;**\nWe will Tour de P
 arks of the area. One at a time.\n**This Week: *Caney Bottoms Loop Tr in P
 isgah Forest:***\nWe are the Sloth Walking Team: “We will get there when
  we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike groups don’t !
 !\n**the Curmudgeon will lead this event. Up to 12 ppl** are welcome to jo
 in us.\n**https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VqhCQZaH4Vs**\nLength: 2.2 mile\
 ; Accum ascent: 250 ft\nDifficulty: Forest trail with rocks & roots. Some 
 up & down hill. Trekking poles necessary. One stream rock-hop xing.\n**(Th
 is event is NOT for beginners or those with health or balance issues.)**\n
 Optional wading in Cove Crk waterslide pool.\n**One challenging 30 ft rock
 -hop over stream (optional wade).**\nPack towels\, extra socks.\n**Mastica
 ting will be ‘in motion’.**\nDrive time: 20 min\; 6 mile 1-way\nApprx 
 return time: 12:30pm **(=2.75 hrs)**\n**Optional:** Lunch after (TBD)\nWea
 ther Check: Brevard\nWeather cancellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nCarp
 ool contributions appreciated. $2.00 suggested\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE 
 ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 1 driver(s). (=8ppl)\nWe sugge
 st open windows while carpooling. Only you know your own health status so 
 judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health or the health of ot
 hers.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy sh
 oes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nIncessant prattlers wil
 l be assumed to be having an affair. My attempts to quiet the prattlers ha
 s failed. This has become a ‘social networking’ event.\nTHIS IS A DOG-
 PARTICIPANT WALK. This event is NOT for those who are uncomfortable with t
 he antics of fun-loving dogs. Well trained dogs (you don’t have to yell.
 ) can be 'off-leash'. 'On leash' when meeting others. Small (lap)dogs may 
 carpool. Large dogs will drive themselves.\nDogs welcome at Sol de Luna…
 \nDESCRIPTION:\nRemember - hikes led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend to have 
 challenging surprises.\nMountain Trolls are thieves\; Zip your backpacks t
 ight.\nAll walks are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN sa
 fety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: : The organizer of this event is a v
 olunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is on
 ly to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor
  activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees 
 to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners
 \, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or perso
 nal loss which might occur while participating in this activity or while t
 raveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agree
 s to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow inst
 ructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from
  the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected
  on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\n**Pat M contact
 : 828.696.6065 (text\; before day of walk)**\ngordie's contact: curmudgeon
 hiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (text)\n**Pics: ht
 tps://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
