SUMMARY:Cove Creek/Caney Bottom Loop\; the hike
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the ***HFF Trail Trekkers***: We a
 ’gonna get our step-counters a’workin’ !!\nHugh will lead on the Cov
 e Crk Falls and Caney Bottoms Falls\, Up to 10 of you are welcome to join 
 him.\n\\*\\*PARTICIPANTS REQUIRE THE APPROVAL OF THE HIKE ORGANIZER.\\*\\*
 \nLength: 6.5 mi Total\; Accum ascent: 700ft\nPace: 2.5mph\nDifficulty: we
 ll established trail\; challenging short steep slopes to bases of falls.\n
 **WET STREAM XINGS\; BE PREPARED !!!**\n**Optional: swimming at the Campgr
 ound Sliding Rock Pool.**\n**Masticating will be ‘in motion’.**\nDrive
  time: 15 min (1-way).\nApprx return time: 2\;30 pm\nCarpool contributions
  appreciated. $2.00 suggested\nWeather Check: Brevard\, NC\nWAITLISTED PEO
 PLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 1 drivers. (=8ppl)
 \n**Please bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoes
  into the driver's car at the end of the hike.**\n**We suggest open window
 s while carpooling.**\nDESCRIPTION\;\nThis hike takes you on a loop past s
 everal nice waterfalls. Climbs moderately overall\; some of the first clim
 bs are very steep but short. Mostly easy trails with one rough section up 
 from Cove Creek Falls to the trail. Beautiful Pisgah scenery and lush wood
 s abound\, and travels through some nice flats above the Davidson River va
 lley at the base of the Pisgah Ridge. Passes seepage bogs and fern-filled 
 open woods.\nAll hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your 
 OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The organizer of this event is
  a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer i
 s only to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any out
 door activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agr
 ees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Part
 ners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or p
 ersonal loss which might occur while participating in this activity or whi
 le traveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further a
 grees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow 
 instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated 
 from the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images colle
 cted on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\nHugh's cont
 act: (**before** day of hike): (662) 324-2425 (text only)\n**Pics: https:/
 /www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
